{
  "id": "python-stdlib-module",
  "pack": "stack",
  "text": "Name a Python standard library module",
  "note": "A module or package shipped with CPython, including easter eggs and ones removed under PEP 594; third-party packages such as numpy do not count",
  "strip": ["module", "library", "python", "import", "stdlib", "standard", "lib", "package"],
  "answers": [
    { "a": "antigravity", "t": "mlion", "q": "Import it and your browser opens xkcd 353. The standard library has an easter egg, and it's a webcomic." },

    { "a": "os", "t": "baseline", "q": "Files, paths, environment variables: the operating system, through a keyhole." },
    { "a": "sys", "t": "baseline", "q": "The interpreter's own settings: argv, path, stdin, and the exit button." },
    { "a": "math", "t": "baseline", "q": "math.sqrt(-1) raises an error. NumPy returns nan, and cmath returns 1j." },
    { "a": "random", "t": "baseline", "q": "A Mersenne Twister. Fine for shuffling a dataset, wrong for passwords." },
    { "a": "json", "t": "baseline", "aka": ["json.decoder", "json.encoder", "json.tool"], "q": "Tuples come back as lists and integer keys come back as strings." },
    { "a": "re", "t": "baseline", "aka": ["regex", "regular expressions"], "q": "Regular expressions, as in: now you have two problems." },
    { "a": "datetime", "t": "baseline", "q": "The module and its main class share a name, so datetime.datetime is a rite of passage." },

    { "a": "this", "t": "overfit", "q": "import this prints the Zen of Python. The text is stored ROT13-encoded in the module itself." },
    { "a": "itertools", "t": "overfit", "q": "Typed to look clever. product, permutations, chain and groupby are the ones you'll really use." },

    { "a": "time", "t": "indist" },
    { "a": "collections", "t": "indist", "aka": ["collections.abc"], "q": "Counter, defaultdict, deque, namedtuple, OrderedDict." },
    { "a": "functools", "t": "indist", "q": "lru_cache, partial, reduce, wraps: tools for functions that take functions." },
    { "a": "pathlib", "t": "indist", "q": "Paths as objects: Path('data') / 'train.csv', with no os.path.join." },
    { "a": "typing", "t": "indist", "q": "Hints that Python itself ignores at runtime." },
    { "a": "subprocess", "t": "indist", "q": "Runs other programs. shell=True with user input is a security hole." },
    { "a": "argparse", "t": "indist", "q": "Turns a script into a command-line tool, with --help for free." },
    { "a": "logging", "t": "indist", "aka": ["logging.handlers", "logging.config"] },
    { "a": "pickle", "t": "indist", "q": "Can run arbitrary code when loaded. Never unpickle a stranger's file." },
    { "a": "csv", "t": "indist" },
    { "a": "copy", "t": "indist", "q": "copy.deepcopy: the cure for 'why did my list change?'." },
    { "a": "string", "t": "indist", "q": "Constants like ascii_lowercase and Template. The str methods live on str itself." },
    { "a": "glob", "t": "indist" },
    { "a": "shutil", "t": "indist" },
    { "a": "threading", "t": "indist", "q": "Real threads, but in standard builds the GIL lets only one run Python bytecode at a time." },
